        "title": "Show HN: Sesame - a local-first, open-source password manager",
        "link": "https://usesesame.app/",
        "description": "<p>I have been working on Sesame, an open-source password manager that keeps your vault local by default. You don't need an account to create or use a vault, and the hosted service never receives the vault itself.\nIt's still early software and the independent security review isn't finished yet, so I am mainly interested in feedback, testing, and people looking through the code.<p>(Linux support is yet to be released on v0.1.2, but currently is in the works.)</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49483038\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49483038</a></p>\n<p>Points: 16</p>\n<p># Comments: 10</p>",
